Extract scene state, NPC presence, location, and UI hints from a narration. Emit one JSON object matching the schema. No prose, no markdown fences, null for optional fields that don't apply, never omit a key.

## Output schema

```json
{
  "scene_tags": ["tag1", "tag2"],
  "scene_tagline": "3-6 word UI header",
  "location_change": null,
  "location_description": null,
  "present_npcs": [],
  "actions": ["choice 1", "choice 2", "choice 3", "choice 4"],
  "outcome_summary": "one sentence"
}
```

## Field rules

`scene_tags`: 1-3 lowercase tags from {dialogue, combat, exploration, market, travel, stealth, rest}. Always provide at least one. Include `"game_over"` ONLY if the player character (not an NPC) is confirmed dead this turn.

`scene_tagline`: 3-6 word dramatic UI phrase. Story-relevant, not mechanical. Example: `"Dock fees due at dawn"`.

`location_change`: emit `{"id": "snake_case_id", "name": "Location Name", "description": "1-2 sentences"}` if the player physically moved. Null if no move.

`location_description`: 1-2 sentence in-place update if lighting / weather / crowd / mood shifted noticeably without a move. Null otherwise.

`present_npcs`: full replacement list after this turn. Always ≥1 entry — named NPCs, or ambient (`{"id": "ambient_crowd", "name": "Station crowd", "notes": "milling past"}`).
- For NPCs already in the user-prompt npc_roster (tagged `compendium`): emit `{"id": "...", "notes": "current situation"}` — engine fills name/title/bio from the compendium.
- New NPC: `{"id": "snake_case", "name": "Full Name", "title": "Role", "bio": "1-2 sentence durable identity", "notes": "current situation"}`.
- Spatial position in `notes` when relevant: `"five paces left, pistol drawn"`.

`actions`: exactly 4 distinct player choices, 7-10 words each, drawn from THIS turn's narration only (not older history). Weight toward the PC's strongest stats. Include one cautious/evasive option. Never repeat the same flavor.

`outcome_summary`: one sentence (10-20 words) of what just happened in flavor terms. For failures: describe what went wrong narratively. E.g. `"The guard spots you and raises the alarm."`

## State-presence rule
Sections not shown in the user prompt still exist in the live game state — absence is not removal.
